      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Supporting Shader would allow us people who write shaders access to use global variables in shaders such as SetGlobalColor and SetGlobalFloat. This would allow for more creativity and flexibility in creating more intricate shaders for the community.\nIn fact, in some instances it is impossible to write a shader without access to these methods. For example, some shaders use an addpass and basemap shader, however due to Unity's implementation, the shader's properties in the inspector cannot reach past the initial main shader, and the additional 2 shaders have no access to the properties, thus limiting the ability to customize the shaders. This could easily be taken care of if global variables were supported.\nThe only current solution to this problem is to create a script added to the object, which allows to set the value, and hard codes (writes the value) into the actual file when it's changed. Quite ugly and clunky workaround.\nWe could seriously use this, please hear us VRChat team\nhttps://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Shader.html",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
