      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As of build 1258, we're now able to globally declare variables, so long as the variable names have the prefix \"_Udon\". However, that leaves the second half of this canny unattended to, that being the global keywords.\nIt's still not possible to declare global keywords. Which means we've either got to use dynamic branching or manual variants for cases where it's not possible to assign keywords directly, e.g. replacement shaders. And for the cases where we can set keywords on materials, we'd still have to loop over every material in order to enable/disable it for all of them.\nThe main concern with global keywords is probably the global keyword limit though, so maybe that'll have to wait until VRChat migrates to Unity 2021.2 or greater.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
